From: lavachemist <48248311+lavachemist@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: let a static port map use the highest port

qcom_swrm_stream_alloc_ports() bounds the port number with
maxport = ctrl->nports, but the ports are numbered 1..nports (bit 0 of
port_mask is reserved at probe, pconfig has nports + 1 entries). Since
6ccec91c3535 ("soundwire: qcom: Fix port exhaustion check in
stream_alloc_ports") turned the check into pn >= maxport, a slave whose
static port map points at the highest port is refused with "All ports
busy" (-EBUSY) every time.

On SM8550 the TX master has qcom,din-ports = 4 and the WCD938x TX slave
maps its DMIC4..7 port to master port 4 (qcom,tx-port-mapping = <2 2 3 4>),
so no DMIC4..7 capture could start. Use nports + 1 as the bound: the
static map can reach port nports, and find_first_zero_bit() still returns
nports + 1 when every port is taken, which the check catches. Tested on
the Retroid Pocket Nova, whose built-in mic is DMIC6.

Fixes: 6ccec91c3535 ("soundwire: qcom: Fix port exhaustion check in stream_alloc_ports")
---
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -1259,7 +1259,8 @@
 			continue;
 
 		port_mask = &ctrl->port_mask;
-		maxport = ctrl->nports;
+		/* Ports are 1-based (bit 0 is reserved), so 1..nports are valid. */
+		maxport = ctrl->nports + 1;
 
 		list_for_each_entry(s_rt, &m_rt->slave_rt_list, m_rt_node) {
 			slave = s_rt->slave;
